course: dictionary
lesson: 1729
title: Civilian: ordinary people, not soldiers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A civilian is a person who is not in the army, navy, air force or police. Civilians are ordinary people, such as teachers, shopkeepers, children and families. Soldiers are trained to fight, but civilians are not.
explain: As an adjective, civilian means to do with ordinary people rather than soldiers. A soldier who leaves the army returns to civilian life, and he may wear civilian clothes instead of a uniform.
explain: Read the context to find the meaning. «Unlike a playground scrap, many ordinary people, called civilians, lose their homes, their safety or their lives.» The words «ordinary people» and «called civilians» tell you that civilians are people who are not soldiers.
fact: A civilian is a person who is not in the army, navy, air force or police.
fact: As an adjective, «civilian» means to do with ordinary people, as in «civilian clothes» and «civilian life».
fact: A soldier who leaves the army returns to civilian life.
fact: In a war, «civilians» are the ordinary people, such as children and families, who are not fighting.
fact: «Civilian casualties» means ordinary people who are hurt or killed in a conflict.
exercise: «Unlike a playground scrap, many ordinary people, called civilians, lose their homes, their safety or their lives.» Who are the civilians in this sentence? | Army generals giving orders | Soldiers who are fighting | Police officers on duty | *Ordinary people who are not soldiers
exercise: What does «civilian clothes» mean? | *Ordinary clothes, not a uniform | Camouflage clothes for the jungle | Clothes worn by a king | Clothes for swimming
exercise: Which of these people is a civilian? | A pilot in the air force | *A postman | A police officer | A soldier in the army
test: Is a police officer a civilian? | Yes, always | Only on their day off | *No, police officers are not civilians
test: What does «civilian life» mean? | Life in a palace | Life in the army | Life under the sea | *Ordinary life, away from the army
exam: Which phrase means the same as «civilians» in a war? | air force pilots | police | *ordinary people who are not fighting | soldiers
